he matching renderer transport even when its mode and identity are unchanged, preventing an open WebSocket from continuing to use the previous endpoint or authentication state."},{"markdown":"Legacy API sends retain one resolved connection configuration for URL, authentication, capability probing, fallbacks, event streaming, and cancellation.","startLine":82,"endLine":82,"text":"Legacy API sends retain one resolved connection configuration for URL, authentication, capability probing, fallbacks, event streaming, and cancellation."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/hermes.ts#sendMessage]] accepts the main-process-owned snapshot selected by `send-message` IPC. Concurrent direct-Remote runs therefore cannot inherit a later UI selection or each other's credentials; inactive SSH remains blocked before tunnel preparation.","startLine":84,"endLine":84,"text":"src/main/hermes.ts#sendMessage accepts the main-process-owned snapshot selected by send-message IPC. Concurrent direct-Remote runs therefore cannot inherit a later UI selection or each other's credentials; inactive SSH remains blocked before tunnel preparation."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/session-location-store.ts#recordSessionLocation]] stores validated tuples in the global desktop directory, independent of the currently selected profile database, and uses atomic writes without credentials.","startLine":88,"endLine":88,"text":"src/main/session-location-store.ts#recordSessionLocation stores validated tuples in the global desktop directory, independent of the currently selected profile database, and uses atomic writes without credentials."},{"markdown":"Unreadable or newer session-location documents remain untouched and reject writes, preventing best-effort metadata recording from replacing recoverable history with an empty store.","startLine":90,"endLine":90,"text":"Unreadable or newer session-location documents remain untouched and reject writes, preventing best-effort metadata recording from replacing recoverable history with an empty store."},{"markdown":"Persisted metadata retains separate records when two connections or profiles produce the same Agent session ID, survives module reloads, deduplicates exact tuples, and rejects incomplete identities.","startLine":94,"endLine":94,"text":"Persisted metadata retains separate records when two connections or profiles produce the same Agent session ID, survives module reloads, deduplicates exact tuples, and rejects incomplete identities."},{"markdown":"Live-run lookup requires connection, profile, and session ID to match, so a colliding session ID cannot activate a run belonging to another machine or profile.","startLine":98,"endLine":98,"text":"Live-run lookup requires connection, profile, and session ID to match, so a colliding session ID cannot activate a run belonging to another machine or profile."},{"markdown":"Focused checks cover independent status classification and the credential boundary for the new registry snapshot.","startLine":102,"endLine":102,"text":"Focused checks cover independent status classification and the credential boundary for the new registry snapshot."},{"markdown":"Local, Remote, and SSH records report separate health and authentication outcomes, retain connection-specific capability evidence, and never return stored API keys.","startLine":106,"endLine":106,"text":"Local, Remote, and SSH records report separate health and authentication outcomes, retain connection-specific capability evidence, and never return stored API keys."},{"markdown":"A running default-home gateway reports Local online in Settings without `gateway.pid` only for the default profile, after validating its process fingerprint. Named profiles without a dedicated API listener stay offline.","startLine":110,"endLine":110,"text":"A running default-home gateway reports Local online in Settings without gateway.pid only for the default profile, after validating its process fingerprint. Named profiles without a dedicated API listener stay offline."},{"markdown":"Settings checks API reachability for the default Local gateway after confirming its process is live. Named profiles keep PID-based status so a read-only status probe never invokes their port allocator or rewrites config.","startLine":114,"endLine":114,"text":"Settings checks API reachability for the default Local gateway after confirming its process is live. Named profiles keep PID-based status so a read-only status probe never invokes their port allocator or rewrites config."},{"markdown":"The default profile's Local API uses its explicitly configured `platforms.api_server.extra.port` when present, otherwise the historical default port; resolving it does not modify configuration.","startLine":118,"endLine":118,"text":"The default profile's Local API uses its explicitly configured platforms.api_server.extra.port when present, otherwise the historical default port; resolving it does not modify configuration."},{"markdown":"Hermes One never claims to stop a multiplex gateway owned by a service or other process; its Stop action reports that the gateway must be managed by its owner.","startLine":122,"endLine":122,"text":"Hermes One never claims to stop a multiplex gateway owned by a service or other process; its Stop action reports that the gateway must be managed by its owner."},{"markdown":"An API key cannot be rotated in Hermes One while another process owns the live default gateway, because that process would keep using its old key until its own supervisor restarts it.","startLine":126,"endLine":126,"text":"An API key cannot be rotated in Hermes One while another process owns the live default gateway, because that process would keep using its old key until its own supervisor restarts it."},{"markdown":"An externally managed gateway's recorded home and the desktop's home can differ lexically through a symlink while naming the same directory; status and control ownership must recognize that equivalence.","startLine":130,"endLine":130,"text":"An externally ma